"""
Road load on a translational flange: aerodynamic drag, rolling resistance and road grade, with
no mass of its own.

The force taken at `flange` is the whole road load, positive when it opposes forward travel:

    F = 1/2 rho CdA v|v| + f_r m g cos(alpha) sign(v) + m g sin(alpha),    tan(alpha) = grade

Aerodynamic drag uses the `v*|v|` form (`ForceDirection = false`) so it opposes motion in both
travel directions rather than always braking forward. Rolling resistance and the grade force
share the single `grade` input — `RollingResistance` reads it as `inclination` (tan of the road
angle) to shed the cosine of normal load, and `GradeForce` reads it as the gradient of the
along-slope gravity term. The stdlib regularizes the sign of rolling resistance near standstill.
Every reaction goes to the road through `ground`.

Being mass-free, the road load moves only as its flange is moved: by the mass in `VehicleBody`,
or by a speed source that follows a planar body's velocity. `m` enters only through the normal
load and the along-slope weight. Source tags: (textbook) standard physical values; (assumed) the
course's choice, the Lecture 1 car.
"""
component RoadLoad
  "Moves with the vehicle; the road load acts here"
  flange = Flange() {^flange}
  "Road gradient, tan(alpha)"
  grade = RealInput() {^grade}
  # f_nominal is negative so the quadratic force acts as a load (drag) rather than a
  # propulsion: the stdlib source drives what its flange moves with -flange.f, and its own
  # docstring states a negative nominal force is what makes it oppose motion in the positive
  # direction.
  drag = TranslationalComponents.Sources.QuadraticSpeedDependentForce(ForceDirection = false, v_nominal = v_nominal, f_nominal = -0.5 * rho * CdA * v_nominal ^ 2) {^drag}
  rolling = TranslationalComponents.Components.RollingResistance(fWeight = m * g) {^rolling}
  cr_const = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = f_r) {^cr_const}
  gradeforce = VehicleSystemsComponents.Vehicle.GradeForce(m = m, g = g) {^gradeforce}
  "Road reference for the resistance reaction forces"
  ground = TranslationalComponents.Components.Fixed() {^ground}
  "Vehicle mass; the road load uses it for the normal load and the along-slope weight (assumed)"
  parameter m::Dyad.Mass = 1400.0
  "Aerodynamic drag area (Cd * A) (assumed)"
  parameter CdA::Area = 0.63
  "Air density at sea level (textbook)"
  parameter rho::Density = 1.2
  "Speed at which drag equals its nominal value; it scales the stdlib law and does not change the drag force (assumed)"
  parameter v_nominal::Velocity = 30.0
  "Rolling resistance coefficient (assumed)"
  parameter f_r::Real = 0.012
  "Gravitational acceleration, standard gravity (textbook)"
  parameter g::Acceleration = 9.80665
relations
  connect(flange, drag.flange) {^id8}
  connect(flange, rolling.flange) {^id9}
  connect(flange, gradeforce.flange) {^id10}
  connect(drag.support, ground.flange) {^id11}
  connect(rolling.support, ground.flange) {^id12}
  connect(gradeforce.support, ground.flange) {^id13}
  connect(cr_const.y, rolling.cr) {^id14}
  connect(grade, rolling.inclination) {^id15}
  connect(grade, gradeforce.grade) {^id16}
metadata {
